WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940
Here is how you use Texas Scraper Kit with an agent.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:06.760
Download version one point zero point two, unzip it, and open that folder

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:11.860
as your agent's project. Your agent needs permission to read files, run commands,

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.840
and reach the internet. Python three point eleven or newer must be installed.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.340
This example uses Codex in the terminal.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:22.040
The interaction shown here comes from an actual run, with selected output and

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.033
shorter pauses.

00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:25.813
Start with the question you want answered.

00:00:25.813 --> 00:00:29.293
Tell the agent to read AGENTS dot M D, install the kit, and

00:00:29.293 --> 00:00:32.993
find three appraisal records matching Space Exploration.

00:00:32.993 --> 00:00:35.873
Ask for a saved summary and official source links.

00:00:35.873 --> 00:00:39.093
You can copy this exact prompt from the page below the video.

00:00:39.093 --> 00:00:42.793
The human supplies the question. The agent works out the commands from the

00:00:42.793 --> 00:00:44.533
instructions included in the folder.

00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:49.353
The agent reads the guide and installs the purchased source in a virtual

00:00:49.353 --> 00:00:53.573
environment. Then it checks the version and runs the owner search.

00:00:53.573 --> 00:00:55.733
These are commands from that agent session.

00:00:55.733 --> 00:00:59.593
The search reaches the county's live appraisal service and saves three records.

00:00:59.593 --> 00:01:02.073
You do not have to type these commands yourself when your agent can

00:01:02.073 --> 00:01:05.408
run them. The command line is how the agent uses the kit.

00:01:06.208 --> 00:01:08.988
Now the agent reads the saved records.

00:01:08.988 --> 00:01:13.628
These three accounts list Space Exploration Technologies Corp as the owner, with addresses

00:01:13.628 --> 00:01:17.848
on Esperson Street. Each record includes its county source link.

00:01:17.848 --> 00:01:21.328
Three matches are a starting point for research, not an inventory of everything

00:01:21.328 --> 00:01:24.968
the company owns. The useful output is a file you can keep, plus

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:27.742
an explanation you can read without knowing the command line.

00:01:28.542 --> 00:01:31.442
The agent also reports what it could not check.

00:01:31.442 --> 00:01:35.322
In this run, the browser permission was declined, so the agent could not

00:01:35.322 --> 00:01:38.702
independently verify the first parcel on the detail page.

00:01:38.702 --> 00:01:42.702
The scraper query itself succeeded. The report distinguishes those two things.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:46.162
It flags empty fields and unverified acreage, and it does not turn an

00:01:46.162 --> 00:01:49.682
appraisal value into a purchase price. You can follow the saved official links

00:01:49.682 --> 00:01:50.617
for that next check.

00:01:51.417 --> 00:01:56.497
Here is the finished answer from the agent, with all three parcel links.

00:01:56.497 --> 00:02:00.617
It also saved a summary document alongside the raw records.

00:02:00.617 --> 00:02:04.237
That is the workflow: give your agent the folder, ask a question, and

00:02:04.237 --> 00:02:06.937
have it return findings with sources and files.

00:02:06.937 --> 00:02:09.897
You can then ask a follow-up question, narrow the search, or take the

00:02:09.897 --> 00:02:11.492
saved records into your next task.

00:02:12.292 --> 00:02:17.412
We started with Texas because development projects raise questions about land and businesses,

00:02:17.412 --> 00:02:21.392
from data centers and energy infrastructure to Starbase.

00:02:21.392 --> 00:02:25.332
The kit gives your agent commands for supported public-record sources.

00:02:25.332 --> 00:02:29.352
Download Texas Scraper Kit from c four five seven three dot org, open

00:02:29.352 --> 00:02:33.672
the extracted folder, and ask your agent to read AGENTS dot M D.

00:02:33.672 --> 00:02:36.908
The page includes the prompt and the actual results from this session.
